==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named by {{w|Christopher Columbus}} after Saint {{w|Martin of Tours}}. The name is sometimes suggested to be a modification of a native {{der|en|awd-taa|-}} (Taino or Kalinago) name {{m|und|Madinina||island of flowers}}<ref>{{cite-book|de|year=2012|author=Antje Schrammel|title=Martinique - Geschichte und Sprache|publisher=GRIN Verlag|isbn=9783656111917|page=4}}</ref> or {{m|und|Matinino||island of women}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌmɑː(ɹ)tɪˈniːk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Martinique.wav|a=Southern England}}

